@nsobid-41EAE379C103E9A512CFA931BA400E938B3B7C55

# Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// Application::init builds its sead::GameFrameworkNx::CreateArg with
// isTripleBuffer (+0x1D) set, which initializeGraphicsSystem hands to
// sead::DisplayBufferNvn::setTripleBuffer; that sets the NVN window
// texture count to 3. Passing false instead selects 2, so the CPU can run
// at most one frame ahead of scanout, cutting a frame of input latency.

@enabled
00539A50 01008052   // MOV W1,#0 for setTripleBuffer (was LDRB W1,[X19,#0xBD])
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2
// (al + agl + sead, NVN). The retail build keeps its symbol table; every
// site was located by symbol and byte-verified against the IDB before
// being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
